WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.254
Federal contract waste.

00:00:02.204 --> 00:00:04.193
The procurement pattern.

00:00:04.193 --> 00:00:06.488
ArriveCAN is not unique.

00:00:06.488 --> 00:00:08.204
It is the pattern.

00:00:08.204 --> 00:00:18.340
Federal procurement consistently produces contracts that balloon far beyond original estimates, deliver late or not at all, and result in zero accountability for the officials who approved them.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.932
Phoenix Pay cost over two point four billion dollars.

00:00:21.932 --> 00:00:25.977
The Canadian Surface Combatant program exceeds sixty billion.

00:00:25.977 --> 00:00:29.693
McKinsey consulting contracts total hundreds of millions.

00:00:29.693 --> 00:00:33.068
Each failure is documented by the Auditor General.

00:00:33.068 --> 00:00:35.579
Each produces recommendations.

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:38.113
Zero produce consequences.

00:00:38.113 --> 00:00:44.920
The lobbying industrial complex ensures that the same contractors who failed on previous contracts bid on and win the next ones.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.624
The waste table.

00:00:46.624 --> 00:00:51.397
Major federal contracts compared by original estimate versus actual cost.
